{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.data Datablocks.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.data Datablocks.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bpy.data datablocks bpy.data datablocks","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.data Datablocks.md","fileName":"bpy.data Datablocks.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"bpy.data Datablocks","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Python Data and Operations]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Python Data and Operations","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.data Datablocks.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.data Datablocks.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bpy.data datablocks bpy.data datablocks","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.data Datablocks.md","fileName":"bpy.data Datablocks.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"bpy.data Datablocks","heading":"bpy.data Datablocks","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"`bpy.data` exposes Blender's internal datablocks, including objects, meshes, materials, textures, images, and scenes. Datablocks separate an object's identity and placement from the underlying data that defines its geometry or appearance.\n\nDirect datablock access is declarative: assigning a named object's location overwrites that property rather than applying a relative transformation to whatever happens to be selected. It is also a stable way to retrieve data by name, inspect nested relationships, create new data containers, or remove unused ones.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Python Data and Operations","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.data Datablocks.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.data Datablocks.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__n